  sections: [
    Section(
      title: 'Initial Presentation',
      content:
          'A 22-year-old female is transferred to acute inpatient rehabilitation following a T12 burst fracture with ASIA A paraplegia sustained when she jumped from a highway overpass 4 weeks ago. She underwent posterior spinal instrumentation and fusion T10-L2. She was medically cleared by the trauma surgery team and psychiatrically cleared by the inpatient consultation-liaison psychiatry team for transfer to rehabilitation. Her psychiatric clearance notes indicate: major depressive disorder (severe, recurrent), borderline personality disorder traits, history of non-suicidal self-injury (cutting) since age 14, and one prior suicide attempt at age 19 (intentional medication overdose requiring ICU admission). She was started on fluoxetine 40 mg daily and quetiapine 100 mg qHS during the acute hospitalization. The psychiatrist notes she is "no longer acutely suicidal but remains ambivalent about survival" and recommends intensive psychological support during rehabilitation. She arrives on the rehab unit making minimal eye contact, answering questions with single words.',
