    Section(
      title: 'History & Systems Review:',
      content:
          '**Psychiatric History:**\n- Major depressive disorder diagnosed age 16, multiple medication trials (sertraline, escitalopram, bupropion — partial responses)\n- Borderline personality disorder traits: emotional dysregulation, unstable relationships, chronic emptiness, non-suicidal self-injury (cutting forearms) since age 14\n- Prior suicide attempt: age 19, acetaminophen overdose requiring N-acetylcysteine treatment and ICU admission\n- Current attempt: jumped from overpass after breakup with boyfriend of 3 years who discovered she was self-harming again. She called 911 herself within minutes of jumping.\n- Outpatient treatment: intermittent therapy compliance, no consistent therapist. Had been seeing a DBT-trained therapist for 6 months before the attempt (last session 2 weeks prior)\n\n**Current Medications:** Fluoxetine 40 mg daily, quetiapine 100 mg qHS, gabapentin 300 mg TID, docusate/senna, subcutaneous heparin, acetaminophen PRN (pharmacy flagged — limited quantity per dose, no bottles at bedside given overdose history).\n\n**Social History:** College senior (communications major) — was 6 credits from graduation. Lives in a college apartment alone (was living with ex-boyfriend until 2 months ago). Parents divorced when she was 8. Mother lives locally, is involved but "overwhelmed" per social work. Father is minimally involved (lives out of state, history of alcohol use disorder). Has a younger brother (age 19) at a different college. Small friend group at school. No employment currently. Health insurance through mother\'s employer.\n\n**SCI Details:** T12 ASIA A complete paraplegia. Neurogenic bladder (indwelling Foley, planned intermittent catheterization transition). Neurogenic bowel (program to be initiated). No sacral sparing. Intact upper extremities. DEXA scan shows low bone density (osteopenia — relevant given age and injury mechanism).',
