    Section(
      title: 'Physical Examination Findings:',
      content:
          '**General:** Thin (BMI 19), appears younger than stated age. Multiple healed linear scars on bilateral forearms (non-suicidal self-injury). Avoids eye contact. Answers questions with 1-2 word responses. No spontaneous conversation.\n\n**Neurological:** T12 ASIA A complete paraplegia. Upper extremities 5/5 throughout. Lower extremities 0/5 throughout. Sensation absent below T12. Bulbocavernosus reflex absent. No voluntary anal contraction.\n\n**Musculoskeletal:** Surgical incision T10-L2 healing well, staples removed. Upper body strength intact but deconditioned. No upper extremity contractures.\n\n**Skin:** Healed linear scars on bilateral volar forearms (multiple, parallel, various stages of healing — most recent appear several weeks old). No active wounds besides surgical incision. No pressure injuries. Ischial tuberosities intact.\n\n**Functional Status:** Moderate assist for bed mobility, maximal assist for transfers, unable to propel wheelchair (has not yet attempted). Dependent for all lower body ADLs. FIM score 52/126.\n\n**Mental Status:**\n- PHQ-9: 18/27 (moderately severe depression)\n- Columbia-Suicide Severity Rating Scale (C-SSRS): Denies current suicidal ideation (intensity 0), but endorsed "passive death wish" — "I don\'t want to kill myself, but I wouldn\'t mind if I didn\'t wake up"\n- Beck Hopelessness Scale: 14/20 (moderate hopelessness)\n- Affect: flat, constricted range. Tearful when asked about the events leading to the attempt.\n- Insight: "I know jumping was stupid. But I still don\'t know why I should try to get better."',
